[gd_scene load_steps=20 format=3]

; P0 CAMPAIGN-SAFE ROUND 3
; Phase B mode inherits res://modes/logspire_leap/logspire_leap_v3_recovery_camera.gd
; Mode V5 is a thin adapter over res://modes/logspire_leap/logspire_leap_v4_phase_b.gd
; Phase B combat inherits res://modes/logspire_leap/logspire_combat_safety_v2_recovery_protection.gd
; Keep Phase A/B gameplay and stable recovery/collision layers load-critical.
; Graphics Phase 2/3 and the Wild Moments water adapter remain source-only.
; Water V16 keeps V15 direct Vine Rescue while compacting only the visible upper Z6 water slab.
; WaterSubmergeWatchdog V2 blocks false water rewinds while the racer is on/recently left the authored Safe Route.
; LadderSystem V6 is compatibility-only and removes ladder/root-stair recovery props.
; JumpRebalance V4 keeps Titan vertical accessibility and moves the CP5+ spiral outward so upper decks do not fold over the climb corridor.
; JumpGapGuard V3 keeps the upper Titan flow bridges, widens CP5->upper-deck access, and adds a flat landing shelf over the destination lip.
; PlayerManualThrottle removes neutral auto-cruise only in Round 3.
; CrownNestFinish treats the destination platform itself as the R3 finish area.
; Phase3Director V7 keeps the V6 upper portal and also clears the blocked mid-Titan spiral jump corridor.
; PlatformGameplay V2 preserves Finale swing timing while replacing Z6 cylinders with flat box boards.
; SkyFinaleVisualPolish V2 now reads the compact Z6 water bounds and masks the remaining channel edges.
; Mode V5 promotes direct/F6 Crown Nest finish into Round Recap -> Round 4 and seeds four AI Finale contenders.
; JumpCollisionAudit runs only after the final geometry/collision layers exist.
